## 4. How do you think containerization changes the way software developers and IT operations teams work together (DevOps)?


I think containerization can make the work between software developers and IT operations teams easier and more consistent. One problem that can happen during software development is when an application works on the developer's computer but does not work correctly on another computer or server. Containers can help reduce this problem because the application and its required dependencies can be packaged together.

From what I learned in this activity, Docker allows an application to be created and managed in a consistent environment. For example, I was able to pull an Nginx image and run it using Docker commands without manually installing and configuring Nginx on the Ubuntu environment. The same container image can also be used in another compatible environment.

This can help developers because they can focus on building and testing the application, while IT operations teams can use the same container image for deployment. It can also make deployment easier to repeat because the same commands and configuration can be used.

For me, containerization shows how development and operations can work more closely together. Instead of manually configuring every server, teams can use containers and automation to make the deployment process more consistent. I also learned that DevOps is not only about using a specific technology. It is also about communication, collaboration, automation, and making the process of developing and deploying software more efficient.

